Subject: Bootstrap difference between means
Message-ID: <6.2.0.14.2.20050201103914.03471348@129.15.69.4>

I have a very simply problem that, while I can think of a way to do it, I 
can't think of an elegant way.

Here's a simplified version: I have two vectors or different lengths, m and 
n. I wish to generate a bootstrap object of the difference between their 
means.  But, I can't think of how to do it elegantly.

I can get there (I think) if I use two separate bootstrap commands to 
generate R replicates of the mean of the m-vector and R replicates of the 
mean of the n-vector. I then save only the replicates, and generate a 
bootstrap object of  their mean difference.

This seems a major hack, though, and I can't help thinking there must be a 
better way. Is there? If so, what is it?

Kim Elmore
