From greg.snow at ihc.com  Tue Feb  1 17:04:45 2005
From: greg.snow at ihc.com (Greg Snow)
Date: Tue, 01 Feb 2005 10:04:45 -0700
Subject: Re: Bootstrap difference between means
Message-ID: <s1ff5578.002@lp-msg1.co.ihc.com>

Look at the group option in the bootstrap function.  Just stack your 2
columns on top of each other and create a factor of the same length
indicating which elements come from which group:

# untested, but should work:
new.xy <- c(x,y)
which.xy <- rep(1:2, c( length(x), length(y) ) )

myboot <- bootstrap(new.xy, mean(new.xy[which.xy==1]) -
mean(new.xy[which.xy==2]),
  group=which.xy)

This should work for you.  You might also want to download the new
resample library from the Insightful web page, it has a new bootstrap2
function designed specifically for 2 sample problems.

