From: BNewquist at constellagroup.com (Brian Newquist)
Date: Fri, 04 Feb 2005 10:25:32 -0500
Subject: Recoding variables in S+
Message-ID: <1BF5A584BBD24645A0524FA419524BCB0ACA8AA1@banyan.constellagroup.com>

Hello,

 

I have two separate questions concerning the recoding of
variables for which I am seeking answers.

 

First Question:

 

Is there a way recode variables based on arrays?  

In particular, is there a method in S+ that would be
comparable to the following SAS code?  

 

***
RECODE FROM 1/2 -> 0/1 (1 = YES) ***;

 
array  old a b c d;

 
array new  a01  b01 c01 d01;

 
do over old;

        
if old = 1
then new = 1;

   
else if old = 2
then new = 0;

 
end; 

 

Second Question:  

 

