One trick is to use `index' as the row indices, and generate column indices,
then use both:

mytest2 <- function() {
    m <- 3
    n <- 4
    rindex <- c(1,1,1,2,2,2,2,3,3)
    cindex <- unlist(lapply(table(rindex), function(i) rep(1:n, length=i)))
    theData <- c(8.6,NA,7.2,5.4,4.9,NA,8.5,6.7,4.6)
    mtx <- matrix(data=NA,ncol=n,nrow=m)
    mtx[cbind(rindex, cindex)] <- theData
    mtx
}

Here I'm assuming the row indices are in order, with no skips.  Otherwise
you need to work a bit harder.

Andy

