From rmh at temple.edu  Mon Feb  7 16:40:01 2005
From: rmh at temple.edu (Richard M. Heiberger)
Date: Mon, 07 Feb 2005 11:40:01 -0500
Subject: Re: How to change a data structure?
Message-ID: <7697435f.caf7fa0a.821e000@po-d.temple.edu>

This is even simpler.  It subscripts the valid positions in the 
result and assigns the observed values to those positions.

Rich

mytest <- function(theData, index, n.col) {
  tmp <- table(index)
  tmp <- rbind(tmp, n.col-tmp)
  result <- matrix(nrow=n.col, ncol=ncol(tmp))
  position <- rep(rep(c(TRUE, FALSE), ncol(tmp)), as.vector(tmp))
  result[position] <- theData
  t(result)
}

n.col <- 4
index <- c(1,1,1,2,2,2,2,3,3)
theData <- c(8.6,NA,7.2,5.4,4.9,NA,8.5,6.7,4.6)

mytest(theData, index, n.col)

