Dear S+ List

I'm very delighted at the responses I recieved from S+ experts, 
and therefore would like to convey a zillions appreciations and
thanks to these wonderful people particularly to Dr. Jo Jiao,
Dimitrios Rizopoulos, Dr. Richard M. Heiberger, Dr. Andy Liaw, 
Alan Hochberg, Steve Riley and Patrick Burns.

Below are the summary of selected functions which work perfectly 
on my problem:

----------------------------------------------------------
1. By Dr. Jo Jiao [his function demonstrates a solution
exactly similar to the required form]
----------------------------------------------------------

ChangeStructure <- function(dat, nr)
{
        #dat---the data set you want the column named "x" to be changed. The 
data set shall
        # at least contain two columns: a column named i and a column named x.
        #nr---the maximum number of repeated measurements for each subject.
        ##################################################################
        cds <- by(dat$x, dat$i, t)
        for(j in 1:length(cds)) {
                if(length(cds) < nr)
                        cds[[j]] <- c(cds[[j]], rep(NA, nr - length(
                                cds[[j]])))
        }
        rownames <- attributes(cds)$dimnames$INDICES
        cds <- unlist(cds)
        cds <- matrix(cds, byrow = T, ncol = nr)
        dimnames(cds) <- list(rownames, paste("xi", 1:nr, sep = ""))
        cds
}
> tempdat
  i   x 
1 1 8.6
2 1  NA
3 1 7.2
4 2 5.4
5 2 4.9
6 2  NA
7 2 8.5
8 3 6.7
