As we wrap this up, it's worth pointing out the importance of this
particular problem (and its minor variants) in clinical data analysis.

The Clinical Data Standards Interchange Committee (CDISC, www.cdisc.org )
has recently developed the Study Data Tabulation Model (SDTM) for data from
pharmaceutical clinical trials.  These tabulations tend to have a "vertical"
format like the input data described by Mr. Khalid.

In order to do useful statistical analysis, the SDTM data often needs to be
transformed into a more "horizontal", tabular format.  This list thread
provides a very useful set of examples of how this can be accomplished.

I happen to be a member of the CDISC Analysis Data Model (ADaM) team with a
strong interest in this area.  While the CDISC standards are to be
"package-agnostic", SAS of course casts a long shadow.  As S-Plus makes
inroads into the pharmaceutical data analysis field, it's good to have these
examples close at hand.

