On Wed, 9 Feb 2005 ahussein at uwindsor.ca wrote:

> unfortunately, rchisq(5, 2, ncp=3) isnot working in my splus2000 (ncp not
> matched).

Where did you see that it exists?  Not on the help page, I am sure.

> I would like to know if there is faster way to generate them than using
> sum of squared normal rvs...

Probably not for df=2, definitely for large df.

For df >= 1, take the sum of one squared normal and a central chisq(df-1).

For df < 1, take the sum of a noncentral chisq(0) plus a central chisq (df).
A noncentral chisq(0) can be simulated by

rchisq0 <- function(n, ncp)
{
    r <- numeric(n)
    K <- rpois(n, ncp/2)
    p <- K > 0
    r[p] <- rchisq(sum(p), df = 2*K[p])
    r
}

