Oh dear!  You are confusing apply (see its help page, it applies to 
matrices or arrays) with sapply.  Please do read the help provided: 
?apply says

   X
          an array (not a data frame; see Note below). Missing values (
          NAs) are allowed if FUN accepts them.

...

   If x is a data frame, it is coerced to a matrix using as.matrix. This
   may give surprising results, e.g. if there are any factor columns then
   the result is character, and any missing values are converted to the
   ordinary character string "NA". To operate on columns use sapply ; to
   operate on rows consider using numerical.matrix to explicitly convert
   to a numerical matrix.

May I recommend consulting a good book as before posting?  (Venables & 
Ripley (2002), for example.)

