Dear S-Users,

I have an xyplot() where different plotting symbols are used for 
subgroups. How can I fit separate regression lines for every subgroup?

So far, I can only plot the overall fitted line.

The code looks like this:

trellis.device()
sps<-trellis.par.get("superpose.symbol")
sps$pch<-1:7
trellis.par.set("superpose.symbol",sps)

spl <- trellis.par.get("superpose.line")   
sps$lty <- 1:7  # use different line types
trellis.par.set("superpose.line",spl)          

xyplot(sqrtax~sowndiv|GRASS+treatment,
groups=LEG,data=axframe,layout=c(2,2),
panel=function(x,y,subscripts,...){panel.superpose(x,y,subscripts,...);panel.lmline(x,y)})

Thank you very much for your help!

Regards
Christioph

From rmh at temple.edu  Thu Feb 10 14:31:28 2005
From: rmh at temple.edu (Richard M. Heiberger)
Date: Thu, 10 Feb 2005 09:31:28 -0500
Subject: Re: xyplot() and panel.superpose
Message-ID: <4067065.cc77b4cc.82d2700@po-d.temple.edu>

> panel=function(x,y,subscripts,...){panel.superpose(x,y,subscripts,...);panel.lmline(x,y)})
>  

Your panel function must be modified to use the subscripts argument in the
panel.lmline() function call.

You can look at my recent book
                Statistical Analysis and Data Display
       An Intermediate Course with examples in S-PLUS, R, and SAS
                Richard M. Heiberger and Burt Holland
and the online files at
   http://springeronline.com/0-387-40270-5

One of the options in ancova function illustrated in Section 10.6, specifically
Figure 10.11 on page 293, does what you are looking for in the case of
   y ~ x * group

While I didn't do the more general case that you have of
   y ~ x | a*b, group=group
I think looking at our code will give you the necessary hints on how
to design the panel function for your situation.

