You can submit splus scripts batch from SAS.  Following is some sample SAS code that creates SAS data sets, which pass information (in this case a counter) to a SAS data set.  batchgraph.ssc is set up to read this and then do some stuff.  SAS iteratively calls this file when the macro one is executed.

options noxwait;

%let part1="C:\Program Files\Insightful\splus62\Splus.bat";

libname dd1 "D:\XXXXXXXX";

%macro one;

%do i=1 %to 54;

data dd1.bat;

col1=%sysevalf((1000*(&i-1))+1);

col2=%sysevalf(&i*1000);

output;

run;

x "%bquote(&part1) START -cwd D:\XXXXXXXX -input D:\XXXXXXXX\batchgraph.ssc -output D:\XXXXXXXX\batchgraph.txt -logfile D:\XXXXXXXX\batchgraph.log -quitonerror";

%end;

%mend one;

