From andrew_white at hmsa.com  Mon Feb 14 18:58:30 2005
From: andrew_white at hmsa.com (Andrew White)
Date: Mon, 14 Feb 2005 08:58:30 -1000
Subject: One solution: Consolidate a DataFrame of Detailed Events: using seq() and match() together
Message-ID: <8B9604D41941A14F90E094B07713F953218095@HON10036.corp.hmsa.com>

After firing off my help message, I got one response but it did not summarize anything directly.

So I banged my head against the desk some more and came up with one solution.

Solution method in brief: 

the trick is using seq() to "index" a dataset, and using match() with the index to look up values of one variable matched to values of another variable. 

------------------------------------------------------------------------

S-Plus Data Consolidation by Name and Associated Attribute

Objective: Summarize total prescriptions per doc where each doc has an associated specialty label 

          from a datasource of individual drug prescriptions identifying doc, specialty and amount prescribed

Setup: start with a dataframe named tdf with oh say 20,000 records

           the records represent all individual prescriptions for the docs of interest; 

           each record has been trimmed to show just:  docname, docsplty, and adjscripts (aka, prescription volume)

Part A. Create a Lookup Table of Provider Names Associated with Specialty Label 

1. Create List of Unique Names

> tname<-unique(tdf$docname)

2. Create List of SeqIDs in tdf corresponding to the Names in tname

> tseq<-tdf$seq[match(tname, tdf$docname)]

3. Create list of Specialties (not unique) that are pulled from records matching the tseq record IDs

> tsplty<-tdf$docsplty[match(tseq, tdf$seq)]

4. Merge the 2 vectors (names & specialties) together to create our Lookup table

> tnamesplty<-data.frame(tname, tsplty)

Part B. Generate the statistical summary for Provider Name & add in Associated Specialty label from Lookup table 

5. Generate numeric summary table

> tsummary<-as.data.frame(tapply(tdf$adjscripts, docname, sum))

> names(tsummary)<-c("tadjscripts")

> tsummary$docname<-row.names(tsummary)

6. Finally add the splty to the summary by matching the names between tsummary and tnamesplty dataframes:

> tsummary$docsplty<-tnamesplty$tsplty[match(tsummary$docname,

tnamesplty$tname)]

