From andy_liaw at merck.com  Thu Feb 17 01:55:45 2005
From: andy_liaw at merck.com (Liaw, Andy)
Date: Wed, 16 Feb 2005 20:55:45 -0500
Subject: Re: transforming 2D matrix to 4D array
Message-ID: <3A822319EB35174CA3714066D590DCD50994E707@usrymx25.merck.com>

If your columns are already sorted in the right way, just make the matrix
into an array and aperm() as needed.  Here's an example:

> m
  A1.B1.C1 A2.B1.C1 A1.B2.C1 A2.B2.C1 A1.B1.C2 A2.B1.C2 A1.B2.C2 A2.B2.C2
1        1        3        5        7        9       11       13       15
2        2        4        6        8       10       12       14       16
> ma <- array(m, dim=c(2, 2, 2, 2))
> ma
, , 1, 1

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    1    3
[2,]    2    4

, , 2, 1

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    5    7
[2,]    6    8

, , 1, 2

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    9   11
[2,]   10   12

, , 2, 2

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]   13   15
[2,]   14   16

> aperm(ma, c(1,4:2))
, , 1, 1

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    1    9
[2,]    2   10

, , 2, 1

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    5   13
[2,]    6   14

, , 1, 2

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    3   11
[2,]    4   12

, , 2, 2

     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    7   15
[2,]    8   16

Andy

